[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m [response] To find \(\cot 90^\circ\), we need to understand the definition of the cotangent function and the value of the tangent function at \(90^\circ\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 1. **Definition of Cotangent:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    The cotangent of an angle \(\theta\) is defined as the reciprocal of the tangent of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \cot \theta = \frac{1}{\tan \theta}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 2. **Value of \(\tan 90^\circ\):**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    The tangent of an angle \(\theta\) is defined as the ratio of the sine of \(\theta\) to the cosine of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \tan \theta = \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    At \(\theta = 90^\circ\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \sin 90^\circ = 1 \quad \text{and} \quad \cos 90^\circ = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    Therefore:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \tan 90^\circ = \frac{\sin 90^\circ}{\cos 90^\circ} = \frac{1}{0}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    Division by zero is undefined in mathematics.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 3. **Conclusion:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m    Since \(\tan 90^\circ\) is undefined, \(\cot 90^\circ\) is also undefined.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Thus, the value of \(\cot 90^\circ\) is \(\boxed{\text{undefined}}\).
