[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m [response] To determine the number of ways to put 4 indistinguishable balls into 2 distinguishable boxes, we can use the "stars and bars" theorem. This theorem is useful for solving problems of distributing indistinguishable objects into distinguishable bins.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m The "stars and bars" theorem states that the number of ways to distribute \( n \) indistinguishable objects into \( k \) distinguishable bins is given by the binomial coefficient \( \binom{n+k-1}{k-1} \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
