[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m First, we factor the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ x^2 + x - 6 = (x + 3)(x - 2) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Setting the denominator equal to zero gives us:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ (x + 3)(x - 2) = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m This equation is satisfied when:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ x + 3 = 0 \quad \text{or} \quad x - 2 = 0 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ x = -3 \quad \text{or} \quad x = 2 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m These are the points where the function is undefined. To confirm that these points are vertical asymptotes, we need to check that the numerator does not also become zero at these points. The numerator is a constant, 2, which does not become zero for any value of \( x \).
