[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m [response] To find the radius \( r \) of the circle inscribed in triangle \( ABC \), we can use the formula \( r = \frac{A}{s} \), where \( A \) is the area of the triangle and \( s \) is the semi-perimeter of the triangle.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m First, calculate the semi-perimeter \( s \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ s = \frac{AB + AC + BC}{2} = \frac{12 + 14 + 16}{2} = 21 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Next, we use Heron's formula to find the area \( A \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m where \( a = 16 \), \( b = 14 \), and \( c = 12 \). Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ A = \sqrt{21(21-16)(21-14)(21-12)} = \sqrt{21 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdot 9} = \sqrt{6615} = \sqrt{63 \cdot 105} = \sqrt{63 \cdot 3 \cdot 35} = \sqrt{63 \cdot 3 \cdot 5 \cdot 7} = \sqrt{9 \cdot 7 \cdot 5 \cdot 7 \cdot 3} = 21\sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Now, we can find the radius \( r \):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[ r = \frac{A}{s} = \frac{21\sqrt{15}}{21} = \sqrt{15} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
