[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m First, we factor the denominator:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[x^2 + x - 6 = (x + 3)(x - 2)\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Setting the denominator equal to zero gives us:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m \[(x + 3)(x - 2) = 0\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m This equation has solutions \(x = -3\) and \(x = 2\). These are the points where the function is undefined, and thus, they are the locations of the vertical asymptotes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1898318)[0m Therefore, the function \(y = \frac{2}{x^2 + x - 6}\) has 2 vertical asymptotes.
